  {
    "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
    "id": "10528",
    "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10528",
    "key": "AIN-205",
    "fields": {
      "summary": "Remove canonical submissions in favor of versioned submission evidence",
      "description": {
        "type": "doc",
        "version": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "User-authorized removal of CanonicalSubmission and its relationships. Backend implementation supporting existing submission review story AIN-95 and parent AIN-3; supplements AIN-18/48/50/51/54, does not close their broader obligations."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Acceptance: remove shared ORM model/exports/associations and all runtime canonical table reads/writes; use immutable pipeline outputs and saved workbench revisions as submission data sources. Preserve schema pin/validation metadata with source evidence; pricing consumes current saved values and records exact source identity/hash. Dashboard, manual creation/backfill, reference finalization and purge work without canonical rows. Preserve existing quotes, signatures and bound snapshots unchanged. Preserve legacy canonical payloads/pins as immutable migration artifacts before dropping table; abort on unresolved ownership or reconciliation failure. Test migration idempotency and recovery, version edits/restore, tenant isolation and pricing/signing regressions with disposable PostgreSQL. Typecheck/ESLint/Prettier in affected packages; record gaps explicitly. Update model documentation and package rollout instructions. No new UI workflow or visual placement change intended; if that changes, capture Before evidence before editing and add interaction coverage."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Required order: ownership/source contract (AIN-48/50/51 slices), package readers/writers and application consumers, legacy migration and reconciliation (AIN-54 slice), integration verification. AIN-18 revision provenance slice included. Excluded broader regeneration comparison UI, global financial stale propagation, board pagination, party identity/claim onboarding and unrelated finance domain tickets: not required to remove this duplicate store and remain outstanding. No production rollout authorized or claimed."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
